SUMMARY:Natural Ornaments - Family Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Decorate for the holidays naturally with acorns\, pine cones\, milkweed pods\, and more! Use your imagination to craft your own unique ornament with materials that nature supplies. Celebrate your creative work with cider or hot cocoa! All materials included. \nCost: $16 ($14 Household & above Members) per child; no fee for accompanying adult \nAges: 5 & up with accompanying adult \nAllergens: Tree nuts\, such as hickory nuts and walnuts\, may be present as craft material. \nNOTE: Children must be accompanied and assisted by an adult. We will be using hot glue guns (low heat) to create most ornaments. \nRegister here!
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/natural-ornaments-family-workshop/
LOCATION:North Carolina Botanical Garden\, 100 Old Mason Farm Road\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27517\, United States
CATEGORIES:Special Events
GEO:35.901081;-79.031939
