SUMMARY:Fiddleheads: Preschool Nature Explorers – Spring Series
DESCRIPTION:Let curiosity lead the way! In this playful\, nature-based drop-off program\, preschoolers will discover the wonders of the natural world through hands-on activities\, outdoor adventures\, seasonal crafts\, storytelling\, and play. \nLed by our youth education staff\, each week explores a new theme inspired by seasonal happenings in the Garden—designed to foster joyful connection with the natural world. \nA healthy snack is included. Group limited to 10. \n\nCost (for entire series): $172 ($154 Household & above Members) \nAges: 4-5 \nNOTE: Children must be able to use the bathroom independently. \nFiddleheads Preschool Nature Explorers is a weekly outdoor program for ages 4-5 at the NC Botanical Garden\, with stories\, sensory play\, and discovery in the garden. Spots are limited! \nRegister here!
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/fiddleheads-preschool-drop-off-spring/2027-04-14/
LOCATION:North Carolina Botanical Garden\, 100 Old Mason Farm Road\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27517\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncbg.unc.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/963/2026/11/PXL_20261014_183853373-scaled.jpg
GEO:35.901081;-79.031939
