UID:10000894-1807869600-1807873200@ncbg.unc.edu
SUMMARY:Nature Tales Story Time
DESCRIPTION:Bring your little one for a morning or afternoon of stories\, songs\, and outdoor discovery! Nature Tales is a monthly family program for children ages 3-7 and a grown-up\, where a nature-themed story comes to life through hands-on exploration in the garden.\n Who? Children ages 3-7\, with an adult When? 10 a.m. to 11 a.m. or 3:30 p.m. to 4:30 p.m. Where? North Carolina Botanical Garden Cost? $5 per child (free for members and families receiving SNAP benefits) \nKnow a family who’d love this? Share the event!  \nUpcoming Dates:\nFriday\, December 11th – Where Did Everyone Go? \nWhere do animals go when winter arrives? Some migrate\, some hibernate\, some stay busy all winter\, and some find cozy places to hide. After the story\, head outside to look for clues that animals are still around\, even when we don’t see them! The program will happen rain or shine\, with indoor activities if the weather is unfavorable. Register here for morning session or afternoon session. \nFriday\, January 15th – Who’s Been Here? \nWho’s been visiting the Garden? Become a nature detective as we read stories\, look for clues like tracks\, scat\, feathers\, and other signs of animal activity\, and discover which wild neighbors might be nearby. Then bundle up and join us for a walk to search for evidence of animals in the Garden! Register here for morning session or afternoon session. \nFriday\, February 26th – Bird Bonanza \nFlap your wings and get ready to explore the wonderful world of birds! Through stories\, movement\, and discovery\, we’ll investigate feathers\, nests\, and the many ways birds find food and make their homes. Then we’ll head out into the Garden to look and listen for our feathered friends! Register here for morning session or afternoon session. \nFriday\, March 19th – Secret Life of Salamanders \nSlippery\, slimy\, and full of surprises! Join us for stories and activities as we discover the fascinating world of salamanders and learn why these secretive amphibians love damp\, hidden places. Then grab a dip net and join us on an adventure to explore a secret vernal pool and see what creatures we can find hiding beneath the water! Register here for morning session or afternoon session. \nFriday\, April 16th – Colors of the Rainbow \nRed\, orange\, yellow\, green\, blue\, and purple—let’s go on a colorful adventure! Through stories and playful activities\, we’ll explore the colors of the rainbow and discover how nature paints the world around us. Then we’ll head outside for a Garden color scavenger hunt to see how many rainbow colors we can find! Register here for morning session or afternoon session. \nFriday\, May 21st – Down by the Stream \nWhat’s crawling\, swimming\, and wiggling beneath the water’s surface? Join us for stories and activities as we discover stream creatures like crayfish\, dragonfly babies (called nymphs)\, and other fascinating aquatic insects. Then grab a dip net and join us for a hands-on adventure at the Meeting of the Waters stream! Be ready to get wet! Participants should wear clothes and shoes suitable for wading into the stream up to their knees. Register here for morning session or afternoon session.
URL:https://ncbg.unc.edu/event/nature-tales-story-time/2027-04-16/1/
LOCATION:North Carolina Botanical Garden\, 100 Old Mason Farm Road\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27517\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncbg.unc.edu/wp-content/uploads/sites/963/2026/11/IMG_5861-scaled.jpg
GEO:35.901081;-79.031939
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=North Carolina Botanical Garden 100 Old Mason Farm Road Chapel Hill NC 27517 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=100 Old Mason Farm Road:geo:-79.031939,35.901081
END:VEVENT
